# Rapid Design System — Agent Rules

## What This Is
Design token pipeline. JSON → CSS variables + utility classes + framework adapters. One source of truth for every UI library. Dark mode is pure CSS via `data-theme` attribute. No JS theming.

## The Golden Rule
Every value traces back to `tokens/base.json`. Never hardcode values in adapters or outputs — always use `var(--rapid-*)` or the `v()` helper.

## File Map

**Source (edit these):** `tokens/base.json`, `dark.json`, `local.json*`, `themes/*.json*`
**Build script:** `scripts/build-tokens.js` — all adapters and utilities defined here
**Other scripts:** `sync-figma.js`, `import-tokens-studio.js`, `generate-dark.js`, `check-contrast.js`, `audit-tokens.js`, `export-native.js`, `migrate.js`, `generate-schema.js`
**Generated (NEVER edit):** everything in `packages/`, `.vscode/rapid-tokens.css-data.json`, `tokens/token-schema.json`
**Tooling:** `demo/`, `tests/`, `figma-plugin/`, `browser-extension/`, `vscode-extension/`

## How To Add a Token
1. Add to `tokens/base.json` → 2. Add dark override to `dark.json` if differs → 3. `npm run build`
Auto-generates: CSS var, utility classes, Tailwind preset entry, VS Code autocomplete, console bridge catalog.

## How To Add an Adapter
1. Add builder function to `build-tokens.js` (returns string, uses `v()` and `fileHeader()`)
2. Add `emit()` in `main()`
3. Add to `package.json` exports
CSS template: `--lib-var: ${v("color-brand-primary")};`
JS bridge template: `import { token } from "./_css-vars-bridge"; ... token("color-brand-primary")`

## Key Helpers (build-tokens.js)
`v("key")` → `var(--rapid-key)` | `toCSSVar("key")` → `--rapid-key` | `flatten(obj, prefix)` → entries | `fileHeader(title)` → comment block | `emit(path, content)` → write+log | `sanitizeCSSValue(val)` → validates | `validateTokenKey(key)` → validates | `deepMerge(a,b)` → safe merge | `resolveAliases(obj)` → resolve $-refs

## Naming
CSS vars: `--rapid-{category}-{subcategory}-{name}` (from JSON path)
Utility classes: `.rapid-bg-{slug}`, `.rapid-text-{slug}` (text tokens strip `text-` prefix), `.rapid-border-{slug}`, `.rapid-p-{size}`, `.rapid-px-{size}`, `.rapid-mt-{size}`, `.rapid-rounded-{size}`, `.rapid-shadow-{size}`, `.rapid-opacity-{name}`, `.rapid-z-{name}`, `.rapid-duration-{name}`, `.rapid-leading-{name}`, `.rapid-tracking-{name}`, `.rapid-focus-ring:focus-visible`

## Semantic Aliasing
`$` prefix references another token by dot-path: `"$color.brand.primary"`. Resolved at build time after local.json merge.

## Security (non-negotiable)
- Skip `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` in all object iteration (`isSafeKey()`)
- All CSS values through `sanitizeCSSValue()`, all keys through `validateTokenKey()`
- No `innerHTML` anywhere — use `createElement` + `textContent`
- Wrap `JSON.parse` in try/catch
- Validate colour inputs: `/^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/`

## Testing
`npm test` — 60 unit tests (build output + security invariants)
`npm run test:e2e` — 21 Playwright tests (demo page, dark mode, Chart.js, SweetAlert2, visual regression)
`npm run check:contrast` — WCAG audit | `npm run audit -- ./demo` — governance report

## All Scripts
`build` compile all | `test` unit | `test:e2e` Playwright | `test:all` both | `check:contrast` WCAG | `audit` governance | `sync:figma` Figma pull | `sync` pull+build | `import:tokens-studio` Tokens Studio | `generate:dark` auto dark | `export:native` RN/iOS/Android | `migrate` codemod | `generate:schema` JSON schema | `demo` serve | `pack:preview` npm preview

## Tooling
**Figma plugin** (`figma-plugin/`): Import/Export/Lint. Zero build step.
**Browser extension** (`browser-extension/`): Manifest V3, floating palette inspector, per-domain persistence, share URL.
**VS Code extension** (`vscode-extension/`): Autocomplete, hover, diagnostics, quick-fix.
**Console bridge** (`packages/runtime/console.js`): `window.rds` API — `rds.get()`, `rds.set()`, `rds.dark()`, `rds.list()`, `rds.search()`, `rds.diff()`, `rds.reset()`, `rds.export()`, `rds.import()`, `rds.help()`.

## Do NOT
- Edit `packages/` (generated) | Use JS context for theming | Hardcode values in adapters | Add UI components | Use `innerHTML` | Skip security guards | Add npm dependencies to core build
